(x)$ by substituting the identified components and their derivatives.\n<ul>\n<li>$f'(x) = (2x)\\sin(x) + (x^2)\\cos(x)$</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\" data-tab=\"Markdown\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-markdown\"># Solution\n<h2>Problem</h2>\n<p>Find the derivative of f(x) = x^2 * sin(x)</p>\n<h2>Answer</h2>\n<p>$$f'(x) = (2x)\\sin(x) + (x^2)\\cos(x)$$</p>\n<p>Apply the product rule formula $f'(x) = u'(x)v(x) + u(x)v'(x)$ by substituting the identified components and their derivatives.</p>\n<h2>Key Steps</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Differentiate the individual components $u(x) = x^2$ and $v(x) = \\sin(x)$ with respect to $x$.\n<ul>\n<li>$u'(x) = \\frac{d}{dx}(x^2) = 2x \\text{ and } v'(x) = \\frac{d}{dx}(\\sin(x)) = \\cos(x)$</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Apply the product rule formula $f'(x) = u'(x)v(x) + u(x)v'(x)$ by substituting the identified components and their derivatives.\n<ul>\n<li>$f'(x) = (2x)\\sin(x) + (x^2)\\cos(x)$\n</code></pre></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\" data-tab=\"Hide\">\n</div>\n</div>\n</div></div>"